235
00:20:44,461 --> 00:20:48,620
to imbue them with a consistent and involving theme,

236
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:50,620
and to build them fast.

237
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:58,460
With so much money at stake and constant pressure to relieve a fickle public of their hard-earned dollars,

238
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:02,980
these steel giants leap skyward with astonishing speed.

239
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:15,160
If we were to wait until we actually had the end product designed,

240
00:21:15,161 --> 00:21:21,860
These buildings would be taking four and five years to build instead of two and three years to build.

241
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:28,000
So what we've had to do is we've had to go after a more universal structure.

242
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:33,360
By universal structures, I mean spaces that have far less columns in them,

243
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:36,800
buildings that have much higher ceilings in them,

244
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:42,160
which give designers much more flexibility as to how they're going to arrange

245
00:21:42,161 --> 00:21:47,900
the non-structural or non-bearing walls inside the movie set.

246
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:49,660
I mean, that's what these are.

247
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:52,920
These are not historical buildings.

248
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:56,560
People will not be coming here 2,000 years from now

249
00:21:56,561 --> 00:21:58,320
and looking at these buildings.

250
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:02,380
This is one large movie set that continually evolves

251
00:22:02,381 --> 00:22:03,840
and continually changes.

252
00:22:03,841 --> 00:22:11,180
suddenly in 1978

253
00:22:11,181 --> 00:22:13,860
Las Vegas faced its worst nightmare

254
00:22:13,861 --> 00:22:16,040
when Atlantic City, New Jersey

255
00:22:16,041 --> 00:22:17,640
legalized gambling

256
00:22:17,641 --> 00:22:19,900
in the years since

257
00:22:19,901 --> 00:22:21,800
gambling has spread to scores of

258
00:22:21,801 --> 00:22:24,380
reservations, riverboats and localities

259
00:22:24,381 --> 00:22:27,960
contrary to original fears

260
00:22:27,961 --> 00:22:29,920
the competition has actually

261
00:22:29,921 --> 00:22:31,500
benefited Las Vegas

262
00:22:31,501 --> 00:22:38,020
As it has grown over the years, Las Vegas has become the place to come.

263
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:39,540
It's the Mecca for gamblers.

264
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,100
There are so many other things going on around the country,

265
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:46,820
but basically all that does is whet the appetites for people to come to the Mecca.

266
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:54,980
The original MGM Grand opened in 1972 was both quasi-film set

267
00:22:54,981 --> 00:22:59,280
and brassy evocation of 1920s movie palaces.

268
00:22:59,281 --> 00:23:06,280
Presenting grandeur with a popular flair, it offered children the magic of movies and

269
00:23:06,281 --> 00:23:09,280
adults the nostalgia of a bygone era.

270
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:18,280
Anticipating huge crowds, the MGM architects turned a dilemma into an opportunity.

271
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:26,280
Designing a massive port cocher, an outdoor awning capable of covering scores of limousines.

272
00:23:26,281 --> 00:23:35,720
At once decorative and functional, the port cocher created the grand entrance, an elegant

273
00:23:35,721 --> 00:23:39,880
ceremony presided over by costumed doormen.

274
00:23:39,881 --> 00:23:43,240
This started a trend.

275
00:23:43,241 --> 00:23:50,340
You'll see in a succession of hotels after that, each port cocher got larger, more glamorous,

276
00:23:50,341 --> 00:23:53,680
more glitzy throughout the 1970s.

277
00:23:53,681 --> 00:24:02,400
In 1980, tragedy struck when a deadly fire swept through the MGM Grand, killing 84 people.

278
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:09,660
During the blaze, some gamblers on hot streaks refused to leave the football field-sized casino

279
00:24:09,661 --> 00:24:17,100
and were finally herded out just minutes before advancing flames consumed its 1,000 slot machines.

280
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:30,260
Today, high-tech monitoring systems make Las Vegas safety procedures among the most stringent in the world.

281
00:24:31,260 --> 00:24:33,340
And there is much to monitor.

282
00:24:34,020 --> 00:24:41,320
A lone mega hotel consumes 15 million gallons of water and 7 million kilowatts of electricity each month,

283
00:24:41,820 --> 00:24:44,600
enough to service over 3,000 homes.

284
00:24:44,601 --> 00:24:53,940
technology helps also to safeguard the profit margin as eye-in-the-sky cameras capture the play at gaming tables

285
00:24:53,941 --> 00:25:03,220
pictures of every table are flashed to a giant control center where they're examined 24 hours a day

286
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:12,100
anyone on a hot streak gets a closer look and has his photo preserved for future reference

287
00:25:12,101 --> 00:25:26,101
with an even greater concentration of huge hotels

288
00:25:31,480 --> 00:25:34,820
Las Vegas has gradually become an urban environment

289
00:25:34,821 --> 00:25:37,680
in the town where car was king

290
00:25:37,681 --> 00:25:40,560
people now walk between competing attractions

291
00:25:40,561 --> 00:25:47,240
The hotels have literally put their front doors right out on the edge of their property

292
00:25:47,241 --> 00:25:52,560
with some kind of big moving sidewalk like into the Mirage or into Caesar's Palace

293
00:25:52,561 --> 00:25:57,840
that scoops you up right at the very edge of the sidewalk and whisks you into the casino.

294
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:02,960
The funny thing about that is, of course, that those moving sidewalks only work one direction.

295
00:26:03,160 --> 00:26:07,440
It isn't like in an airport where you can take a moving sidewalk going both directions.

296
00:26:07,441 --> 00:26:11,100
In Vegas, you can only go in. You're on your own getting out.

297
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:20,400
Whether on foot or in a car, visitors to the strip frequently find themselves trapped with mobs of fellow fun seekers.

298
00:26:22,940 --> 00:26:25,540
Personally, I think gridlock is good.

299
00:26:26,220 --> 00:26:29,560
I think gridlock is part of the reason people come to Las Vegas.

300
00:26:29,860 --> 00:26:31,720
They love to be with other people.

301
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:36,620
This is Times Square almost every night of the year.

302
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:44,440
Like Times Square, in recent years Las Vegas hotels have decided to clean up their act.

303
00:26:44,441 --> 00:26:51,440
Beginning with Circus Circus in 1975, they have actively pursued the family market.

304
00:26:51,441 --> 00:26:55,440
Gone are most of the semi-nude dancing girls.

305
00:26:55,441 --> 00:26:58,440
In are the arcades and the animal acts.

306
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:16,760
In the grand tradition of Las Vegas entrepreneurs, the transition from adult fantasy land to family

307
00:27:16,761 --> 00:27:21,700
resort was spearheaded by one man.

308
00:27:21,701 --> 00:27:28,120
Steve Wynn had a vision that Las Vegas could be something more than just casinos with hotel

309
00:27:28,121 --> 00:27:29,120
rooms.

310
00:27:29,121 --> 00:27:34,420
He showed the industry that they had only just begun to grow.

311
00:27:34,421 --> 00:27:41,380
He was the catalyst that began the building boom where every casino had a new and bigger

312
00:27:41,381 --> 00:27:49,980
and better idea on how to entertain our tourist population.

313
00:27:49,981 --> 00:28:03,981
When the MGM Grand opened in 1993, it took 39 armored cars two nights

314
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:15,480
to move the $3.5 million in quarters necessary to run the casino.

315
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:18,940
Modern Marvels will continue in a moment.

316
00:28:19,980 --> 00:28:24,140
We now return to Las Vegas Hotels on Modern Marvels.

317
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:32,420
In 1977, Vegas pioneer Steve Wynn bought the old Golden Nugget Casino.

318
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:37,980
He promptly added his first hotel wing, threw in a dash of salesmanship,

319
00:28:38,580 --> 00:28:41,280
and revived it as a money-making operation.

320
00:28:42,100 --> 00:28:45,940
Quiet beginning to what became a very loud empire.

321
00:28:49,980 --> 00:28:56,380
Steve Wynn is probably the most demanding client I've ever had.

322
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,880
He's also the best client I ever had.

323
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:04,180
He's willing to put some money up and he supports everyone on the design team.

324
00:29:05,220 --> 00:29:10,480
And he's pushing all the time and always, always looking for a better way.

325
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:15,480
To create the Mirage Hotel in the late 1980s,

326
00:29:15,481 --> 00:29:20,262
1980s, Wynn raised a then unheard of $700 million.

327
00:29:20,263 --> 00:29:23,800
He was building the most costly hotel

328
00:29:23,801 --> 00:29:29,359
in Las Vegas history and gambling on selling a new concept.

329
00:29:29,360 --> 00:29:32,280
With the opening of the Mirage,

330
00:29:32,380 --> 00:29:36,894
Las Vegas took an entirely different direction where it wasn't just about gambling.

331
00:29:36,895 --> 00:29:37,595
It was

332
00:29:37,596 --> 00:29:41,380
about each hotel being an attraction in and of itself.

333
00:29:43,940 --> 00:29:47,080
Wynn envisioned the Mirage as a South Seas paradise,

334
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:52,020
an irresistible tropical playground sprung from the Nevada desert.

335
00:29:52,980 --> 00:29:57,780
With the Mirage, Wynn promised a complete environmental experience

336
00:29:57,781 --> 00:29:59,860
to dwarf even Caesar's Palace.

337
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:03,620
Rather than simply a pleasant backdrop to gaming,

338
00:30:03,621 --> 00:30:07,500
This thematic design was its own form of entertainment.

339
00:30:12,660 --> 00:30:15,800
Wynn boldly presented his new kind of casino

340
00:30:15,801 --> 00:30:19,260
by building the first major street-side attraction in town,

341
00:30:19,780 --> 00:30:22,060
a 40-foot erupting volcano.

342
00:30:23,720 --> 00:30:29,300
The volcano at the Mirage was a challenge that Steve Wynn put on the table,

343
00:30:29,301 --> 00:30:34,780
And that was to say that not even Walt Disney has attempted a volcano yet.

344
00:30:35,560 --> 00:30:37,360
And that was our mandate.

345
00:30:37,720 --> 00:30:43,920
He wanted to see a volcano that, in fact, everyone would believe it was a real volcano.

346
00:30:45,580 --> 00:30:50,460
This volcano had to erupt safely and spectacularly every hour.

347
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:56,100
Regulating the amount of natural gas and triggering it with an electronic ignition

348
00:30:56,101 --> 00:30:58,760
made the explosion controllable.

349
00:30:59,300 --> 00:31:04,300
Attention to detail included scenting the blast with a pina colada aroma

350
00:31:04,301 --> 00:31:09,300
that was both pleasant and suggestive of the South Seas.

351
00:31:11,300 --> 00:31:15,300
What was hard was lighting it. That's what was hard.

352
00:31:15,301 --> 00:31:18,300
Because you have the light, number one, from the explosion,

353
00:31:18,301 --> 00:31:24,300
but in between the explosions, the lighting effect on the tumbling water and on the stonework,

354
00:31:24,301 --> 00:31:28,300
that was by far the most challenging thing.

355
00:31:29,300 --> 00:31:36,960
For much of the Mirage d'Core, Wynne and his design team went with the theory that God is the best architect.

356
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:40,100
Bring in real tropical landscaping.

357
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:48,860
Believing also that nature can always be improved upon, they lit the trees with artificial yet romantic glow.

358
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:58,940
When you see these beautiful, growing, living things, lit so sexy, so subtle, so wonderful,

359
00:31:59,300 --> 00:32:01,880
That's when the imagination begins to happen,

360
00:32:02,080 --> 00:32:05,820
and that's when architecture is at its highest point.

361
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:11,740
For the Mirage High-Rise, one of nature's most precision elements

362
00:32:11,741 --> 00:32:14,100
would be used to create a glittering facade.

363
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:22,020
Each of its 3,000 rooms look out through glass containing 24-carat gold.

364
00:32:23,240 --> 00:32:28,180
Real gold glass doesn't turn green when the blue sky is reflected off of it.

365
00:32:28,181 --> 00:32:34,840
The gold glasses made from copper, when the sun or the sky is reflected off of it, look green.

366
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:37,000
We didn't want the building to be green.

367
00:32:37,780 --> 00:32:38,780
We wanted to be cold.

368
00:32:40,880 --> 00:32:46,860
In 1993, Wynn unveiled a larger-than-life version of every boy's fantasy.

369
00:32:47,840 --> 00:32:49,860
Treasure Island Hotel and Casino.

370
00:32:51,220 --> 00:32:54,000
Here, the sidewalk attraction was Buccaneer Bay,

371
00:32:54,001 --> 00:33:00,200
a Disney-esque pirate village that the pirates of old would have built if they could have afforded it.

372
00:33:03,020 --> 00:33:09,140
Every 90 minutes, each night, a full-scale theatrical presentation plays out in the bay.

373
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:15,700
Audiences find themselves right in the thick of the action as pirates battle a British frigate.

374
00:33:15,701 --> 00:33:18,220
Will you strike your bloody colors?

375
00:33:18,560 --> 00:33:21,540
When I'm in Davy Jones' locker, not before.

376
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:23,040
As you wish, sir.

377
00:33:23,041 --> 00:33:36,620
While Steve Wynn was busy transforming Las Vegas into his version of Disneyland,

378
00:33:37,260 --> 00:33:42,020
others began to realize a hidden secret behind the Magic Kingdom.

379
00:33:44,840 --> 00:33:48,920
If you really look at Disneyland, Disneyland is a shopping center.

380
00:33:48,921 --> 00:33:53,420
people planned vacations around going to a shopping center.

381
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,680
Meaning that if you really take a second look at Disneyland,

382
00:33:58,000 --> 00:34:01,100
it is full of retail and it is full of food and beverage.

383
00:34:01,760 --> 00:34:04,380
Eager to match Disneyland's success,

384
00:34:05,060 --> 00:34:09,240
Las Vegas hotels have vastly expanded their shopping facilities.

385
00:34:10,660 --> 00:34:14,360
The forum shops at Caesars Palace lead the new trend,

386
00:34:14,900 --> 00:34:18,720
offering an array of upscale shops tied together by the setting

387
00:34:18,721 --> 00:34:20,580
a mock Roman street.

388
00:34:23,940 --> 00:34:28,600
The lighting speeds through a 24-hour cycle every three hours,

389
00:34:29,060 --> 00:34:31,060
subtly heightening the excitement.

390
00:34:33,760 --> 00:34:36,680
Freely mixing ancient tales and modern technology,

391
00:34:37,140 --> 00:34:39,660
the Euromall features a statue of Bacchus

392
00:34:39,661 --> 00:34:43,420
that leaps to life in full animatronic splendor.

393
00:34:43,421 --> 00:34:50,040
and in this emporium lack of tradition is a virtue

394
00:34:50,041 --> 00:34:57,520
gambling for dad, shopping for mom, dolphins for the kids

395
00:34:57,521 --> 00:35:02,840
by the 1990s Las Vegas had nearly perfected the family resort

396
00:35:02,841 --> 00:35:09,600
in 1993 Steve Wynn tore down the dunes to make way for his newest hotel

397
00:35:09,601 --> 00:35:17,600
The pirate ship at Treasure Island fired a simulated cannonball across town to the dunes,

398
00:35:17,601 --> 00:35:31,601
where the famed sign and hotel were timed to implode with the cannon blast.

399
00:35:32,600 --> 00:35:38,340
It was a unique show and a spectacular symbol of out with the old, in with the new.

400
00:35:39,820 --> 00:35:43,460
Wynn's innovations have opened the floodgates to bold new ideas,

401
00:35:43,461 --> 00:35:50,160
and the next generation of hotels would meld form and fantasy as never before.

402
00:35:55,700 --> 00:36:00,740
The Caesar shopping complex cost over $100 million to build.

403
00:36:00,741 --> 00:36:04,420
It draws about 30,000 visitors a day.

404
00:36:06,140 --> 00:36:08,200
Modern Marvels will continue in a moment.

405
00:36:11,140 --> 00:36:15,740
We now return to Las Vegas Hotels on Modern Marvels.

406
00:36:21,200 --> 00:36:25,780
Modern Las Vegas is the number one resort destination in the country

407
00:36:25,781 --> 00:36:28,360
and the mecca for serious gamblers.

408
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:31,980
Casinos still vie for the business of high rollers,

409
00:36:32,540 --> 00:36:36,400
the super-rich who think nothing of losing a million dollars in a weekend.

410
00:36:38,660 --> 00:36:44,760
The ornate Pompey suite at Caesar's Palace lists at $7,500 a night,

411
00:36:44,761 --> 00:36:48,160
but invariably is given gratis to high rollers.

412
00:36:50,240 --> 00:36:54,900
They lounge about the four-bedroom duplex amid Baroque columns,

413
00:36:54,901 --> 00:36:59,900
gilded tapestries and Italian frescoes.

414
00:37:00,900 --> 00:37:03,900
Everything that we design, we put a storyline to it.

415
00:37:03,901 --> 00:37:07,900
Whether it's a restaurant, whether it's a shopping center, whether it's a casino,

416
00:37:07,901 --> 00:37:11,900
we create a storyline. So we have a beginning, a middle, and an end.

417
00:37:13,900 --> 00:37:17,900
Each storyline is complemented by the latest technology.

418
00:37:17,901 --> 00:37:21,900
Racing to provide customers with the hottest new thrills,

419
00:37:21,901 --> 00:37:22,601
thrills.

420
00:37:22,602 --> 00:37:27,860
Hotels are constantly upgrading their attractions to boost sensory stimulation.

421
00:37:32,460 --> 00:37:38,080
Sound systems that are in the casinos and in the restaurants are extremely complex.

422
00:37:38,300 --> 00:37:43,460
There's complexes what you might find in any good movie studio. And we actually have

423
00:37:43,461 --> 00:37:49,660
departments and divisions of people who look at sound for these different environments on a

424
00:37:49,661 --> 00:37:50,660
continual basis.

425
00:37:52,660 --> 00:37:57,300
In recent years, the best show in town has become the buildings themselves.

426
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:05,220
1990 brought the 4,000-room Excalibur, an Arthurian extravaganza,

427
00:38:05,221 --> 00:38:10,140
complete with moat, drawbridge, and fire-breathing dragon.

428
00:38:10,141 --> 00:38:24,141
in 1993 the new MGM Grand opened its doors immediately becoming the largest hotel on earth

429
00:38:24,240 --> 00:38:34,540
perhaps the most distinctive building in town is the Luxor Hotel an ultra-modern take on ancient

430
00:38:34,541 --> 00:38:43,229
Egypt. Its 30 stories and 26,783 glass plates shimmer in the desert sun.

431
00:38:43,230 --> 00:38:45,280
Standing guard in

432
00:38:45,281 --> 00:38:51,960
front is a new kind of sign. A giant sphinx scaled 50% larger than the original.

433
00:38:56,160 --> 00:39:03,340
Inside, its atrium takes up 29 million cubic feet, making it the largest in the world.

434
00:39:04,540 --> 00:39:11,220
Even going to one's room is an adventure, with elevators that rise at an angle of 39 degrees

435
00:39:11,221 --> 00:39:15,860
to match proportions devised long ago by Egyptian architects.

436
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:25,780
At night, the pyramid performs a vanishing act.

437
00:39:27,060 --> 00:39:29,260
It's like a black hole in the middle of the strip.

438
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:33,920
Everything else is lights and waving all these megawatts at you to get your attention,

439
00:39:33,921 --> 00:39:38,700
and suddenly there's this totally negative thing, this big black object.

440
00:39:38,980 --> 00:39:40,880
It's almost invisible at night.

441
00:39:42,620 --> 00:39:46,200
The Luxor is topped by the brightest beacon in the world,

442
00:39:46,780 --> 00:39:50,500
40 billion candle power of light shooting into the night sky.

443
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:56,360
Ironically, since light is only visible when it hits something,

444
00:39:56,820 --> 00:39:58,920
and the desert air is especially clean,

445
00:39:58,921 --> 00:40:04,220
This super searchlight does little but cause havoc for pilots flying overhead.

446
00:40:18,720 --> 00:40:24,200
The latest leap in Las Vegas architecture is recreating actual modern cities.

447
00:40:24,201 --> 00:40:29,640
The Hotel Casino New York, New York takes a place well known to millions,

448
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:35,560
transporting its physical presence and bustling atmosphere in startling detail.

449
00:40:38,300 --> 00:40:46,980
The difficulty in creating this project overall was the fact that you didn't want it to come off in a cartoonish fashion.

450
00:40:46,981 --> 00:40:53,980
You wanted the details to be so substantial and so real that people could identify with the project.

451
00:40:54,200 --> 00:40:57,080
in New York City, inside and outside.

452
00:40:58,200 --> 00:41:03,620
The giant facade collected a dozen of the Big Apple's most famed towers,

453
00:41:04,180 --> 00:41:06,460
recreating them at one-third scale.

454
00:41:07,860 --> 00:41:12,780
The Las Vegas version of the Empire State Building stretches 47 stories high,

455
00:41:13,240 --> 00:41:16,300
enough to make it the tallest structure in the city.

456
00:41:16,301 --> 00:41:27,380
the idea that it was a very large project didn't really hit us until we found out that between

457
00:41:27,381 --> 00:41:34,640
this project and the one next door we had consumed all of the number 11 reinforcing bars and 14

458
00:41:34,641 --> 00:41:40,340
reinforcing bars in the country now that's a lot of steel considering that this is these are largely

459
00:41:40,341 --> 00:41:47,900
concrete projects. New York, New York is monumental architecture and perhaps the

460
00:41:47,901 --> 00:41:54,200
biggest piece of pop art in the world. It draws people into a unique environment

461
00:41:54,201 --> 00:42:00,580
surrounding them with Art Deco details of New York in the 1920s.

462
00:42:10,340 --> 00:42:16,280
People from New York really like it, which is so wonderful.

463
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:20,800
And to have those people come here and be happy with it and enjoy it.

464
00:42:21,280 --> 00:42:27,080
We've created everything except the smells and the muggings and all the litter around.

465
00:42:27,240 --> 00:42:29,900
We've tried to eliminate as much of that as possible.

466
